  "overview": {
    "title": "White sand over turquoise water",
    "p1": "The White Dune (Dune Blanche) is a bright sand mass rising at the lagoon’s edge — a short climb that rewards you with views over water, peninsula and desert.",
    "p2": "Most visitors come for late light. The sand is soft; wear closed shoes and carry water. It is a scenery stop more than a long hike.",
    "p3": "Combine with a lagoon shore drive or a kite-spot transfer if you are based at a camp."
